---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AboutCard from "../components/AboutCard.astro";
import Signup from "../components/Signup.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who's writing this build log, why it exists and what to expect from it."
  hasSignup
>
  <div class="about-page wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">← the longer version</p>

    <AboutCard level="h1">
      <p>
        I'm {SITE.author}, a {SITE.location} marketer with about 20 years in the business, a couple of
        kids, and too many cats.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2025 I started building things with AI: Space Invaders, dashboards, now a robot. I'm not
        trying to become an engineer. I just want to be the person who can build the thing instead
        of making a deck about it.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        A public build log. {SITE.tagline} Every other Sunday I publish one entry: what I built with
        AI, what broke, and what I learned fixing it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm writing it in public for two reasons. Explaining a thing is the fastest way to find out
        whether I actually understand it. And if you're starting from the same place I did, the
        wrong turns are probably more useful to you than the wins.
      </p>

      <h2>The scoreboard</h2>
      <p>
        Every entry keeps score: hours spent building, things shipped, things broken, and the number
        of times I had to stop and ask <span class="highlight">"wait, what does that mean?"</span>{" "}
        The totals on the home page add themselves up from each entry. I don't get to fudge them.
      </p>

      <h2>This site is homework too</h2>
      <p>
        I built this site as one of the projects, and the code is public. If you want to see how it
        works, or how many tries it took, the <a href={SITE.githubRepo}>source is on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're on the same road, <a href="#subscribe">come along</a>. One email{" "}
        {SITE.cadence}, and you can start with <a href="/log">the log</a>.
      </p>
    </AboutCard>

    <Signup variant="inline" />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-block: 56px 96px;
  }

  .about-page :global(.signup) {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 639.98px) {
    .about-page {
      padding-block: 32px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
